Z||000000||JSocha||11-22-2001||10:39 PM||||...alot like Christmas!<P>We went up to my parents place today for Thanksgiving.<P>We got back around 7/8PM tonight.<P>Wife is busy putting up Christmas trees and decorating now.  I told her she couldn't start decorating until after November 31st.  She of course wanted to do it after Thanksgiving...but I insisted not until after the 31st and that was final.<P>She finally caught on as to why I didn't want her decorating until after the 31st.  DANG!  Why did she have to look at the calender?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Anyways, 12 Christmas trees this year are going up in the house. Oy Vey!  Last year it was 6.<P>Hope you all had a wonderful Thanksgiving today and that you are all back safe on the forum!<P>And I hope Cheeve and his parents are safe in Texas and enjoying Thanksgiving together.<P>And last but not least to you all, let me be the first to say!<P><FONT SIZE="3"><B><I>SEASONS GREETINGS and HAPPY HOLIDAYS!</I></B></FONT><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||7
Z||000001||Fformula88||11-23-2001||08:27 AM||||I'll say it is, but for another reason.  On my commute into work thismorning, I drive past a big mall and some other stores on the highway.  The parking lots were already jammed!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  This was at quarter to 7 this morning already!!  I always thought trying to shop with the stores so crowded was insanity anyway!<P>I must say the office is nice today anyway.  A lot of people are off, and its quiet enough to get some work done.  (Does posting to PFF count as work?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||11-23-2001||09:04 AM||||Awww   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> BAH HUMBUG Christmas is such a pain. Guess I'll finally have to take down the halloween decorations. They kinda blended<BR>in with the Thanksgiving stuff, but santa on a witches broom, carrying a jack-o-lantern with a turkey chasing him aint going to cut it. Sorry Jsocha, gonna hijack this, sorta.<P>So, how many lights/decorations do you guys put up?  Anybody do the Chevy Chase or Toolman Taylor thing--a really big show?? Outside lighting has gotten so cheap to buy, everybody in San Angelo goes way out, but it is in the older part of town, where Mexico's influence is higher, that the best are located. Beautiful front lawns and a lot of hard work put into those, not just a bunch of gaudy flashing lights.<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierobaby||11-23-2001||10:54 AM||||I had a good thanks giving... if anyone cared... I went to my boyfriends aunt's house and had somethanksgivig time with them. but back to the decorations<P>we put all the outdoor stuff up last saturday because other wise the ground would be to frozen to put anything in it. we will decorate the inside of the housr two weeks befor christmas and put the tream up December 15th or so so I've got time to wait to decorate again||||reg||1
